# 5e-iii — Editar. Sized M/L and split in two on 2026-09-23, on the day it was
# taken and before a line of it was written. `5e.split` had it down as an M, and
# the parent row's own first sentence named the reason it would not stay one —
# *"the price change is the substance, and it has a branch nothing else in this
# app has."* A branch is a form detail; THREE branches under an exclusion
# constraint is a contract with Postgres.
#
# ⚠️ THIS GUARDS NO MIGRATION, the property `5e.split` asserts one level up. 0002
# applied product_family, product_variant and price_list and their SEVEN write
# policies on 2026-08-26 — six of them the insert/update pairs this child edits
# through, and the seventh price_list_delete, which nothing here uses.
# EACH_CHILD_SAYS asserts it POSITIVELY, because merging is automated and a child
# that quietly grows a migration is not a reviewable mistake but a deployed one.
#
# THE SEAM, IN ONE LINE: it is `5e`'s own seam one level down, the move `5d-iv`
# made on 2026-09-22. `5e` divided on the argument that 5e-i is the half a machine
# can hold and the other two are the half only the owner's eye can — and 5e-iii,
# alone of the three, still carried BOTH. 5e-iii-a is the second 5e-i: a module, a
# node suite, a contract check over real HTTP, no screen. 5e-iii-b is the form,
# whose whole instrument is a phone (R9, §2.11).
#
# ⚠️⚠️ AND THE SPLIT IS WORTH MORE HERE THAN SIZE ALONE, FOR 5d-iv's REASON: THE
# TWO HALVES FAIL DIFFERENTLY. The write's mistakes are silent and irreversible in
# the small — a close-and-open whose second call fails leaves a product PRICED
# YESTERDAY AND PRICELESS TODAY, in the middle of a trading morning, done by a
# shopkeeper who was CORRECTING a price rather than removing one. The form's
# mistakes are visible and cost a glance. Putting them in one row means the one
# nothing can see rides in on the back of the one only a person can.
#
# ⚠️⚠️ TWO THINGS WERE NOT IN THE PARENT ROW WHEN IT WAS TAKEN, which is most of
# what the sizing was worth and is the third sizing in a row to find something.
#   * THE ORDER, AND ITS PARTIAL FAILURE. The parent row described the same-day
#     branch and never said that the ordinary branch is TWO calls whose sequence
#     is forced by price_list_no_overlap — nor what the gap between them leaves.
#   * C3.17 vs THE APPLIED SCHEMA. C3.17 says any role may change a price,
#     "client-side only; no schema depends on it", and 0002 makes price_list
#     insert and update has_role(manager). The sentence is false against the
#     database and has been since 2026-08-26. ⚠️ It was parked in the decisions
#     block and it is why 5e-iii-b was GATED and 5e-iii-a was not — RULED the same
#     evening, "leave the fence as is", so both children shipped on 2026-09-23 and
#     no migration came out of it. The gate is history; the reason it existed is not.
#
# ⚠️⚠️ AND THE SPLIT'S OWN CLAIM WAS HALF WRONG, RECORDED HERE BECAUSE IT IS THE
# ONE THING A FUTURE SIZING SHOULD LEARN FROM. This file says 5e-iii-b is the form
# "whose whole instrument is a phone". It is not only that: Editar is FOUR WRITES
# BEHIND ONE BUTTON across two tables with no transaction, and the ORDER they go in
# — plus what a failure between them leaves — are right answers a node suite can
# read. 5e-iii-a's subject was the PRICE alone, so nothing had asked the question.
# EDIT_ORDER, editPlan, editTouches and editLine went into 5e-iii-a's module when
# 5e-iii-b was built, with ten falsification fixtures behind them. **A "pure
# rendering" child is a claim to check on the day it is taken, not on the day it is
# sized.**
SPLIT_ID="5e-iii"
SPLIT_GROUPS=( "5e-iii|5e-iii-a 5e-iii-b" )
DELIVERABLES=(
  # ⚠️ ONE SPELLING PER ROW, and never an alternation: a bare pipe in the regex
  # field truncates the entry and it fails downstream as a DROPPED deliverable,
  # which reads exactly like the defect this list exists to catch.
  #
  # ⚠️ EVERY REGEX MUST ALSO MATCH THE PARENT ROW — assertion 3 refuses a
  # deliverable the parent stopped promising, so that the coverage claim below
  # cannot go vacuous by the parent being tidied.
  #
  # ⚠️ ROWS 1, 3, 4, 6 AND 8 ARE ALSO `5e.split`'s DELIVERABLES on the parent.
  # That is deliberate and not a second home: there they must land in 5e-iii,
  # here they must land in exactly one of its children — the arrangement
  # 5c-iv.split and 5d-iv.split already stand in.
  "the price change, and the dated window price_list holds it to|dated window|5e-iii-a"
  "the order the two calls must go in, and what the gap between them leaves|priced yesterday|5e-iii-a"
  "the tax rate and the pack size, set once and never guessed|tax_rate|5e-iii-a"
  "deactivation rather than deletion — neither catalog table has a delete policy|is_active|5e-iii-a"
  "the contract check over real HTTP — the only instrument the UPDATE fence gets|5e-iii-a-catalog-edit-contract|5e-iii-a"
  "Editar, and everything the four-field form pushed behind it|Editar|5e-iii-b"
  "the switch no pilot screen may expose|C8\.8|5e-iii-b"
  "what becomes of Costos, the third button 5d-iii shipped dead|Costos|5e-iii-b"
  "the dash on La Familia, and whether this is where it turns|amber|5e-iii-b"
)
PHRASES=(
  "5e-iii-a|F|NO SCREEN AND NO COMPONENT|The 5e-i shape and the 5d-iv-a shape, for the reason both gave: 5h.5 owns src/ui/ and comes after the screens that would justify a primitive, and the owner refused ten primitives guessed at against undrawn screens on 2026-09-13. It is also what keeps this child fully checkable — everything it ships has a right answer a node suite or a live round trip can read."
  "5e-iii-a|F|refuses a zero-length range|price_list is a dated range table under an exclusion constraint, and the change a shopkeeper makes twice in one morning is a DIFFERENT write from the one he makes once. Closing the row in force at today makes effective_to equal effective_from when that row started today, and price_list_range_ordered refuses it. A module that knew only the ordinary branch would work all day and fail the second time a price was corrected."
  "5e-iii-a|F|CLOSE BEFORE YOU OPEN|The sequence is forced by price_list_no_overlap, exactly as WRITE_ORDER is forced by the composite foreign keys one child over. Opening the new row first makes two rows cover today and the second is refused — so this is not a preference and not slower the other way round, it is the only order that works. And saying it in the row is what makes the partial failure below a named state rather than a discovery."
  "5e-iii-a|F|A CASHIER IS REFUSED|product_variant_update, product_family_update, price_list_update and price_list_insert are all has_role(manager) in 0002. Nothing in TypeScript has ever read a policy, CREATE POLICY is not in the knowledge graph, and RLS is bypassed by the postgres superuser — so a check that does not set role authenticated passes vacuously. 5e-i's check asserted this on INSERT; nothing has ever asserted it on UPDATE, and UPDATE is the whole of this child."
  "5e-iii-b|F|the owner's phone is the whole instrument|R9 and §2.11. Every judgement left in this child is rendering, navigation or layout, and no check here will ever say it is wrong. A row that does not say so reads like a row something is watching — which is the misreading that put both halves in one task in the first place."
  "5e-iii-b|F|C8.8|enforce_stock is the one switch a pilot screen may never expose, and this form is the only screen in the pilot that would ever have been tempted to offer it. C8.6 guarantees permanent drift in both directions, so turning it on breaks the polleria at the counter in front of a customer."
)
EACH_CHILD_SAYS=(
  "I|ships no migration|0002 applied these three tables and their write policies on 2026-08-26, and nothing in this split reopens the schema. A POSITIVE assertion because merging is automated: a child that quietly grew a migration is repaired only by a fix-forward migration, never by an edit. ⚠️ It matters more in step 5 than it did earlier — 5b.9 is an open row in this same step that DOES ship one, so 'the next task has no migration' has stopped being true of the step as a whole. ⚠️ AND IT IS THE THING THE C3.17 RULING WOULD CHANGE: widening price_list_insert past manager is a migration, which is exactly why it is parked in front of the work rather than inside it."
)
